      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The industry standard generally distinguishes between satire and hate speech based on intent and impact. Satire, even when offensive, often relies on exaggeration or parody to critique power structures. Hate speech, conversely, is characterized by direct attacks or dehumanizing language targeting protected groups, intending to promote violence or discrimination. The key line is often whether the content promotes hatred or merely critiques ideas through humor.",
